Reliable Data Transmission

This project demonstrates clocked data transmission using an Arduino Nano, a data line, a clock line, and a 16x2 LCD display.

Features

- Bit-by-bit data transmission
- Separate clock and data signals
- LCD visualization of transmitted bits
- Adjustable transmission rate

Working Principle
The message "Hello, world" is stored in the transmitter.
Each character is converted into its 8-bit binary representation.
Bits are transmitted sequentially through the data line.
A dedicated clock signal synchronizes data transmission.
The LCD displays:
The complete message on the first row.
The binary representation of the currently transmitted character on the second row.
Each clock pulse indicates when a new bit is available on the data line.

